Agreed.  My first ascension was a Valk, twoweaponing a +7
Grayswandir and a +6 katana.  With an AC of -40 and close to 500
HP.  I just bludgeoned my way through: a couple of wands of
death for Rodney, and melee *everything* else.  (Master mind
flayer: big deal.  Let him come to me; with speed, I'll get two
swipes before his first hit.  Which means he won't get a hit.)
I didn't know half of what I knew now about getting in and out
of the last level quickly, avoiding air elementals, etc.  (Even
on the plane of air, with those weapons, you're only getting
pummeled for about two turns, and with AC -40 and the orb, that
doesn't mean all that many hit points.)

In my experience, you don't usually get it that good, and some
more subtle strategy is needed.  Today, I'll often choose
Magicbane over Grayswandir, especially if I can twoweapon with a
silver saber, a broadsword, or a long sword or a katana.  It's
good enough, if you know what your doing, and it has other
advantages.  (With Grayswandir and the katana, for example, I
didn't know that you had to get to the up stairs to fight the
major demons.  With speed boots, I got two hits before they
could act, and usually, after two hits, they weren't there any
more to act.  Just walk up to Orcus and smack him good.)  But if
he's already got Grayswandir and a saber...

