Since I've started wielding Magicbane, I find that L's aren't
that much of a problem.  I find I generally don't bother with
genocide any more.  (If I find a scroll, I keep it, just in case
I get in a tight spot, rather than use it immediately.)  If he's
got Grayswandir and a good second weapon, both well enchanted,
mind flayers aren't a problem.  Let them come to you, timing it
so you get two swipes when they reach you, and you can melee
them without too much problem.  If I were genociding, the first
thing I'd do is disenchanters.  Unless you're a spell caster, to
get them at a distance without loosing enchantments on your
ranged weapon, I find them to be the biggest pain.

Of course, the first time round... Nothing beats AC -40, the
Valk's quest artifact, something like 500 hit points, and
twoweaponing a highly enchanted Grayswandir and another good
weapon.  That leaves room for lots and lots of stupid mistakes.

